# Interfaces in the server's request container (docs/compiler/codegen.md
# §13). The e2e runner builds the development environment, whose `use` rule
# picks `LoudGreeter`; `Stamp` has a single implementation and no rule; and
# `PublicUrls` builds absolute URLs from the public origin
# (`http://localhost` in this runner).

### the development rule, the single implementation and PublicUrls
POST /bindings.greet.GreetProtocol/Greet
content-type: application/json
connect-protocol-version: 1

{"name": "Ana"}
>>> 200
json {"text": "HELLO, Ana! (stamped)", "home": "http://localhost/home"}
